+# Spec Delta
+
+## Purpose
+Lets people bring many tasks into the list at once from plain text, reporting which lines could not be imported and why.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Lines are read as title, priority and tags
+`importTasks` SHALL read each line of the text as `title;priority;tags`. The priority MAY be empty or omitted, meaning `normal`. The tags MAY be empty or omitted and are separated by spaces. Surrounding whitespace in each field SHALL be ignored. Blank lines SHALL be skipped and never reported. Both `\n` and `\r\n` line endings SHALL be accepted.
+
+#### Scenario: Full line
+- **WHEN** the text is `Renew the insurance;high;admin money`
+- **THEN** one task is added, titled `Renew the insurance`, with priority `high` and tags `admin` and `money`
+
+#### Scenario: Empty priority
+- **WHEN** the line is `Buy milk;;shopping`
+- **THEN** the task is added with priority `normal` and tag `shopping`
+
+#### Scenario: Title only
+- **WHEN** the line is `Call mum`
+- **THEN** the task is added with priority `normal` and no tags
+
+#### Scenario: Blank lines
+- **WHEN** the text contains empty or whitespace-only lines
+- **THEN** they are skipped and not reported as rejected
+
+### Requirement: Result reports what was imported and rejected
+`importTasks` SHALL return `{ imported, rejected }`: `imported` is the number of tasks added, and `rejected` lists, in text order, every non-blank line that could not be added as `{ line, reason }`. `line` is the 1-based line number in the text, counting blank lines. `reason` says what is wrong. A rejected line SHALL NOT stop the import of the other lines.
+
+#### Scenario: Mixed text
+- **WHEN** the text has a valid line, an invalid one, and another valid one
+- **THEN** `imported` is 2 and `rejected` holds one entry with the invalid line's number
+
+#### Scenario: Line numbers count blank lines
+- **WHEN** the text is `A`, a blank line, then `B;urgent`
+- **THEN** the rejected entry has `line` 3
+
+### Requirement: Invalid lines are rejected
+A line SHALL be rejected, and add no task, when its title is empty or too long, its priority is not `low`, `normal` or `high`, its title duplicates a task already in the list (including one imported earlier from the same text), or it has more than three fields. The list SHALL otherwise be unchanged by a rejected line.
+
+#### Scenario: Unknown priority
+- **WHEN** the line is `Pay rent;urgent`
+- **THEN** it is rejected and no task is added
+
+#### Scenario: Duplicate title
+- **WHEN** the same title appears twice in the text, or already exists in the list
+- **THEN** the later line is rejected and the existing task is unchanged
+
+#### Scenario: Too many fields
+- **WHEN** the line is `Call;high;admin;extra`
+- **THEN** it is rejected and no task is added
+
+#### Scenario: Empty text
+- **WHEN** the text is empty
+- **THEN** the result is `{ imported: 0, rejected: [] }`
